{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":5,"timestamp":1779504106,"nonce":"d1Abe8jzxh8VlhYSRKjYFeeuf4Q=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDJ0DjM8AAAAGBkNy2w"},"added":["bug"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779507355,"nonce":"POLbXk8DNRSKGs4neDqjY4ksx08=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDadslw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/166#issuecomment-4524043415"},"message":"## Wrap-up addendum: operator-side log post-mortem\n\nBeyond the symptoms captured in this issue's body, the diagnosis would benefit from a **bag- and operator-log-side post-mortem on both freeze events**.\n\n### Specific log sources to pull\n\n- **Salmon `~/.ros/log/`** — CAMP's own logs at the time of both freezes. Salmon's [§2](../blob/jazzy/docs/logs/2026/2026-05-22_salmon_logs.md) reference the launch directory has timestamped per-launch subdirs; the relevant ones to inspect are the launch active during pre-launch (~16:?? EDT — Event 1) and the launch active mid-mission (~19:37 EDT — Event 2).\n- **Operator bag (`~/data/logs/operator/2026-05-22`)** for any topics CAMP was consuming at the time, in particular costmap topics, diagnostics, and any UI-feedback topics. Cross-correlate timing of last successful message vs first sign of stall.\n- **Salmon's `~/.ros/log/.../launch.log`** specifically — salmon's deployment log §2 notes this is where to look for either a traceback or a SIGKILL indicator.\n\n### Comparative questions to answer\n\n1. Event 1 was during a WiFi-down state — was CAMP's stall caused by a backed-up event queue trying to render data that never arrived, or by a downstream UDP-bridge ERROR state propagating up?\n2. Event 2 was during healthy WiFi — what was the trigger? Costmap update size? A specific message type?\n3. Did both events show similar log signatures (suggesting a single underlying bug), or different ones (two distinct issues)?\n\nIf the answer to #3 is \"different signatures,\" consider splitting Event 2's investigation into its own issue.\n\n### Scope\n\nSmall bag- and log-side analysis; can be combined with the comprehensive power-analysis investigation (sister wrap-up issue) since the analysis agent will already have the bag DBs open.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779766021,"nonce":"qDHMO6O0tNl6JDTsUrPTNbxq0lQ=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDpajCQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/166#issuecomment-4539720457"},"message":"**Post-mortem — root cause UNCONFIRMED. Capturing the next occurrence is the path forward ([`rolker/camp#52`](https://github.com/rolker/camp/issues/52)). Leaving this open.**\n\nI dug into the salmon CAMP logs (`~/.ros/log`), the boat-side bag, and CAMP's source. The honest result: **we cannot confirm CAMP actually froze, let alone why** — and the deeper I looked, the more the hard evidence dissolved into mundane causes.\n\n**What's hard (logs):**\n- **Event 1 (16:30):** CAMP's `SIGKILL` was the launch's normal **SIGINT→SIGTERM→SIGKILL shutdown escalation** after the operator restarted the stack (camp `signal_handler` at 16:29:52 → SIGKILL 16:30:02). **~6 other nodes also needed SIGKILL** in that shutdown — because of an **rmw_zenoh \"close operation timed out\"** hang. So camp's `-9` is *not* evidence of a freeze, and the \"coupled CAMP+udp_bridge death\" was the operator restarting the whole stack.\n- **No OOM** (operator confirmed `sudo journalctl -k` is clean).\n- **Event 2 (19:37):** boat-side, both udp_bridge legs tripped ERROR (19:35–36) and the survey resumed at 19:37:06 with a `path_follower_visualization` burst (0→253/min) + new `/plan`.\n- CAMP runs a `MultiThreadedExecutor` + Qt thread with a `shared_ptr` marker-snapshot handoff.\n\n**What's soft:** the \"freeze\" itself rests on real-time operator/agent perception (not clearly recalled; field logs agent-written). Event 2 is the only event whose signature (alive + solo `pkill` while the stack survived) resists a mundane explanation, but it too is reconstructed, not captured. The link-stress trigger is temporal correlation; the executor↔Qt mechanism is an unproven architectural suspect.\n\n**Why unconfirmable from this data:** a GUI hang leaves no log trace. The only definitive evidence is a **thread backtrace of the hung process** — never captured.\n\n**Path forward ([camp#52](https://github.com/rolker/camp/issues/52)):** a Qt-timer GUI heartbeat (stall while the ROS executor thread is alive = definitive GUI-hang signature) + auto-backtrace on stall, so the **next** occurrence self-documents; plus an operator capture one-liner and an optional bag-replay/`tc netem` bench repro. Until then, treat \"CAMP hangs under link-stress\" as a **hypothesis**.\n\n**Separate finding:** the **rmw_zenoh \"close operation timed out\"** on shutdown forces SIGKILL of many nodes, making every stack restart slow/messy — worth its own issue.\n\nFull analysis: #169 §14. Leaving #166 **open** until the capture confirms or refutes.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779767511,"nonce":"MNe+zfX5P9PfXhHoW3xRbI2RL48=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDphkMg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/166#issuecomment-4539835442"},"message":"**Correction (verified) + the SIGSEGV identified.** Two things in my earlier post need fixing:\n\n1. **The zenoh \"close operation timed out\" is NOT network-caused, and NOT \"every restart is messy.\"** I verified the RMW config on salmon: it's stock rmw_zenoh, **loopback-only** — sessions `connect: [\"tcp/localhost:7447\"]`, `listen: [\"tcp/localhost:0\"]`; the router's `connect` endpoints are empty; multicast scouting is off; no `ZENOH_*_CONFIG_URI` override. Cross-host traffic is udp_bridge, not zenoh. So the dead WiFi router **cannot** affect zenoh session close. And the **healthy 20:27 shutdown was clean** (zero close-timeouts), so it isn't a general per-restart problem either. The 16:30 close-hang is real but its **cause is unverified** (candidate: local `zenohd` unresponsive under the 16:30 high-churn state — *not asserted*). **Downgraded from \"worth its own issue\" to a one-off footnote.** Retracting the network framing in my prior comment.\n\n2. **The `-11` SIGSEGV** in that session was **CAMP segfaulting on shutdown at 20:27** (mission end) — *not* a mid-mission crash and *not* the 19:37 hang. A minor CAMP **teardown** bug, in the same Qt/`MultiThreadedExecutor` teardown area as the hang; noted on [`rolker/camp#52`](https://github.com/rolker/camp/issues/52).\n\nNet for this issue: unchanged — root cause of the freezes remains **unconfirmed**, capture plan in camp#52. The zenoh and shutdown-segfault items are footnotes, not the freeze.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}